7, 2026</span></span></p><h1 class="post__title" data-v-e79ea0f6>Robots in Rugby: Evri set to trial autonomous guided vehicles in its Rugby hub</h1></header><img src="{{ asset('images.prismic.io/ev-mercury/94a05482-5519-4dcc-81b3-7332e50ee1ea_Barnsley%2bImage3dd8.jpg') }}" srcset="https://images.prismic.io/ev-mercury/94a05482-5519-4dcc-81b3-7332e50ee1ea_Barnsley+Image.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;rect=0%2C0%2C1920%2C1080&amp;q=50&amp;fit=max&amp;width=640 640w, https://images.prismic.io/ev-mercury/94a05482-5519-4dcc-81b3-7332e50ee1ea_Barnsley+Image.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;rect=0%2C0%2C1920%2C1080&amp;q=50&amp;fit=max&amp;width=828 828w, https://images.prismic.io/ev-mercury/94a05482-5519-4dcc-81b3-7332e50ee1ea_Barnsley+Image.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&amp;rect=0%2C0%2C1920%2C1080&amp;q=50&amp;fit=max&amp;width=1200 1200w" alt width="960" height="540" class="post__featured-image" loading="lazy" sizes="(min-width: 992px) 50vw, 100vw" data-v-e79ea0f6><section class="post__content" data-v-e79ea0f6><div data-v-e79ea0f6><!--[--><section id="·-------evri-will-trial-two-agv-power-pallets,-in-partnership-with-translift-group" class="section-wrapper rich-text" index="0" data-v-92714c58 data-v-ebc71926><div class="section-wrapper__container" data-v-ebc71926><!--[--><!--[--><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->·       Evri will trial two AGV power pallets, in partnership with Translift Group<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->·       The trial marks Evri’s first step on its ‘under the roof’ robotic journey<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->·       The announcement follows two successful trials of autonomous delivery robots in Yorkshire.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->27th April 2026  <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri Group is looking to lead the way in innovation and automation as the UK’s premier parcel delivery company and has taken the next step on its robotics journey as it has today announced it is trialling two automated guided vehicles (AGVs) at its Rugby hub, marking the first step in what Evri is calling ‘under the roof’ robotics.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Currently, Evri has workers moving cages or pallets with cardboard in from one end of the hub to another all day, every day. The introduction of these robotic vehicles means they can pick up the load, and as a growing business, investing in robotics like this allows<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->existing workers to be redistributed to more productive and meaningful tasks to meet the growing demands of increased parcel volumes as well as being upskilled to become robot handlers!<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->These automated power pallets have a built-in LiDAR (Light Detection Ranging) to detect ceiling mounted sensors which guide and map vehicle’s route. The AGV will be programmed to follow the route from A to B and scheduled stops can be included if needed and on a continuous loop allowing workers to load or unload manually along the way. It carries a load of up to 1.5 tonnes.  They can also be switched from automated to manual if required.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->The announcement comes following successful trials of a robotic delivery dog last August as well as an on-going trial of autonomous deliveries in Barnsley, the UK’s official and only ‘Tech Town’, where Evri’s largest hub is based.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><!--]--><!--]--></div></section><figure id="this-trial-marks-the-first-of-what-we-hope-will-be-many,-exploring-how-robotics-can-support-our-hub-and-depot-operations-as-well-as-the-colleagues-that-work-there.-we’re-constantly-looking-at-innovative-ways-to-improve-and-enhance-what-we-do,-and-we’ve-got-more-exciting-things-we’ll-be-looking-at-this-year." class="quote" index="1" data-v-8c8b68f6><blockquote class="quote__content" data-v-8c8b68f6><p data-v-8c8b68f6>This trial marks the first of what we hope will be many, exploring how robotics can support our hub and depot operations as well as the colleagues that work there. We’re constantly looking at innovative ways to improve and enhance what we do, and we’ve got more exciting things we’ll be looking at this year.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="quote__source" data-v-8c8b68f6><p data-v-8c8b68f6>Adrian Berry, Innovation Delivery Manager at Evri Group</p></figcaption></figure><figure id="i’m-excited-to-see-the-agvs-in-action-and-to-see-the-benefits-they-can-have-on-production.-some-of-the-work-our-colleagues-carry-out-can-be-very-monotonous,-our-hub-is-incredibly-large-and-it-takes-a-long-time-walking-back-and-forth-carrying-cardboard-for-example,--things-like-this-will-help-our-people-on-the-tasks-they-don’t-love-so-they-can-spend-time-on-work-they-enjoy." class="quote" index="2" data-v-8c8b68f6><blockquote class="quote__content" data-v-8c8b68f6><p data-v-8c8b68f6>I’m excited to see the AGVs in action and to see the benefits they can have on production. Some of the work our colleagues carry out can be very monotonous, our hub is incredibly large and it takes a long time walking back and forth carrying cardboard for example,  things like this will help our people on the tasks they don’t love so they can spend time on work they enjoy.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="quote__source" data-v-8c8b68f6><p data-v-8c8b68f6>Lee Moss, Head of Hub operations at Evri Group</p></figcaption></figure><section id="section_component" class="section" index="3" data-v-997ea6a1><div data-v-997ea6a1><h2 class="section__title" data-v-997ea6a1></h2><div class="section__text" data-v-997ea6a1><!--v-if--></div></div></section><section id="about-evri" class="section-wrapper rich-text" index="4" data-v-92714c58 data-v-ebc71926><div class="section-wrapper__container" data-v-ebc71926><!--[--><!--[--><p><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->About Evri<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri Group brings together Evri, DHL eCommerce UK – which in 2026 will be rebranded Evri Premium, a network of DHL - customs clearance and logistics specialist Coll-8 and business letters leader UK Mail, to create the UK’s premier parcel delivery company. The combined Evri Group will deliver more than 1 billion parcels and a further 1 billion business letters annually.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri, the core operating brand, currently delivers around 900 million parcels a year, and is on a mission to be the most convenient way to send, receive and return parcels, without costing the earth.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Working with everyone from Europe’s top retailers, marketplaces and pre-loved sites to gift-givers, the roots of Evri can be traced back to Yorkshire in 1974. The business has grown over the last five decades and now has a team of 12,000+ employees and 30,000+ couriers, as well as a growing network of more than 10,000+ ParcelShops and Lockers and 500+ state-of-the-art hubs and depots.  Following its acquisition of Coll-8, an Irish independent customs clearance and logistics specialist, and merger with DHL eCommerce UK, Evri Group continues to enhance its international capability and enable world trade.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri has over 4 million independent 5-star Trustpilot reviews, an average courier rating of 4.6/5, reflecting a strong commitment to customer experience.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->For more info: <!--]--><!--]--><a href="https://urldefense.com/v3/__http:/www.evri.com/news-and-corporate__;!!KZXpRQ!XXp1b6auPQhqEikzO24Td1WLLcOiKei-_sEGnaz1LXy6FIZdIH744ZKALMLghNBHhvufy1YVkeCCqssIjm9R-A$" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank"><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->www.evri.com/news-and-corporate<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></a><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if--> <!--]--><!--]--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Media enquiries  <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->For any enquiries relating to Evri Group or its companies; Evri, DHL eCommerce UK, UK Mail and Coll-8, please contact: <!--]--><!--]--><a href="mailto:prteam@evri.com" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank"><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->prteam@evri.com<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></a><!--]--><!--]--></p><!--]--><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></div></section><footer class="post__footer" data-v-e79ea0f6></footer></article></div></section><!--]--></main></div></div><div id="teleports"></div><script>window.__NUXT__={};window.__NUXT__.config={public:{ENV_NAME:"prod",PUBLIC_PATH:"https://www.evri.com",WEB_BASE:"https://www.evri.com/",PRISMIC_REPO:"ev-mercury",DEVTOOLS:false,API_BASE:"https://api.hermesworld.co.uk/",AUTH0_USERS_ENDPOINT:"https://hermes-df-prod.eu.auth0.com/userinfo",AUTH0_CLIENT_ID:"dC8K22keYtRszHe7dnmlWSve2kP7mUBF",AUTH0_DOMAIN:"hermes-df-prod.eu.auth0.com",AUTH0_LOGIN_REDIRECT:"https:/